      <div class="article-text-body mt-4">
        <p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Setting up Click-to-WhatsApp on Google Ads is one of the most effective ways to connect high-intent searchers directly on WhatsApp. Many businesses spend heavily on Google Ads yet still lose leads due to slow landing pages or long forms.</span></p>
<p><a href="/auth/register"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Click-to-WhatsApp Ads</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> remove this friction. Instead of filling out a form, users can start a conversation with a business directly on WhatsApp with just a tap on Google Ads. It helps businesses drive higher lead generation and more personalized real-time engagement.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">In fact, 73.3% of consumers prefer communicating with brands via messaging, and 72.4% are more likely to buy from brands that offer messaging. This conversational marketing strategy works great for local businesses, e-commerce stores, healthcare, automotive, and real estate.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">With <a href="/auth/register">HelloBotz</a>, businesses can run Click-to-WhatsApp on Google Ads to turn search ad clicks into WhatsApp conversations and capture high-intent leads.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">In this guide, we will learn how to set up Google Click-to-WhatsApp ads, track results, control costs, and automate replies to drive more sales.</span></p>
<h2 id="what-is-click-to-whatsapp-on-google-ads"><b>What Is Click to WhatsApp on Google Ads?</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Click to WhatsApp on Google Ads is a feature that enables businesses to add a direct WhatsApp message button to their Google Ads through a </span><a rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" href="https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/16669188?hl=en&amp;ref_topic=16669490"><span style="font-weight: 400;">message asset</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. The moment someone taps the button, a WhatsApp chat window opens with a pre-filled message to let users start a conversation or ask questions with businesses.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">It makes it easier for potential customers to connect without waiting for a callback or filling out a form. Here’s how it works:</span></p>
<p><b>Someone searches on Google and sees your ad: </b></p>
<p><b>Path 1: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">If the user clicks the headline, they go directly to your website.</span></p>
<p><b>Path 2:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> If they tap the message button (User clicks the ad → WhatsApp chat window opens with a pre-filled message → conversation starts)</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This feature works well with Search campaigns and Performance Max campaigns. However, the WhatsApp message button does not show alongside call assets or lead form assets.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Plus, Google currently offers this feature in beta, which means it may not be available in every ad account yet. </span></p>
<h2 id="why-run-click-to-whatsapp-on-google-ads"><b>Why Run Click-to-WhatsApp on Google Ads?</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Many businesses invest in Google Ads to attract potential customers. But the thing is, long forms and phone calls often slow down the process and lead to lost leads.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Here’s why Google Click-to-WhatsApp ads stand as a beneficial solution for businesses:</span></p>
<ol>
<li><b> Faster Lead Capture: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">It enables potential customers to ask questions and receive an instant response from businesses with just a single click while buying intent is still fresh.</span></li>
<li><b> Higher Conversion Rates:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Eliminates the need for users to load slow landing pages or find a phone number, which leads to fewer steps and more conversions.</span></li>
<li><b> Better Customer Experience: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">No need to download any extra app. Users can get instant answers to their queries on the app that they already use every day, making the buying journey smoother.</span></li>
<li><b> Lower cost per lead: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">CTWA ads lower your cost per lead by removing traditional conversion friction and capturing verified contact data instantly.</span></li>
<li><b> Automate Customer Conversations:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Businesses can deploy an AI chatbot, connect WhatsApp with their CRM system, and use </span><a href="/resources/blog/whatsapp-automation-tools/"><span style="font-weight: 400;">WhatsApp automation tools</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> to qualify leads, schedule appointments, send catalogs, and follow up with leads automatically.</span></li>
</ol>
<h2 id="google-click-to-whatsapp-ads-vs-meta-click-to-whatsapp-ads"><b>Google Click to WhatsApp Ads vs Meta Click to WhatsApp Ads</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Both Google Ads and Meta Ads help brands generate qualified leads, improve sales, and drive measurable business growth by targeting users at different stages of their buying journey. But both of them work differently. They both open a WhatsApp chat window, but the difference is user intent.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Let’s see a side-by-side comparison of both ad formats to get a clearer picture: </span></p>
