<p><b>When to Use Each?</b></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Use Google click-to-WhatsApp ads when people are actively searching for your product or services. Your ad automatically reaches them when they need it and search for that keyword. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Use Meta click-to-WhatsApp ads when you want to reach people while they are browsing on Facebook or Instagram and encourage them to start a conversation.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Learn </span><a href="/resources/blog/create-click-to-whatsapp-ads/"><span style="font-weight: 400;">how to create Click-to-WhatsApp ads</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> to run them on Facebook or Instagram.</span></p>
<p><b>Can You Run Both?</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Yes, businesses can run both formats of ads. Google ads catch people when they search for your related product or service, while Meta ads build interest. To learn more in detail, go through our complete guide on </span><a href="/resources/blog/whatsapp-ads/"><span style="font-weight: 400;">WhatsApp Ads</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. </span></p>
<h2 id="what-do-you-need-before-you-set-up-a-click-to-whatsapp-google-ad"><b>What Do You Need Before You Set Up a Click-to-WhatsApp Google Ad?</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Message assets are still in beta. This means not every account can use them yet. Here’s all you need before you get started with Google Click-to-WhatsApp ads:</span></p>
