<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Review </span><a rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" href="https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14888522?hl=en"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Google&#8217;s official requirements for message assets</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> before starting.</span></p>
<p><b>Where Can People See Click to WhatsApp Ads on Google?</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Click to WhatsApp ads on Google Ads are widely available globally on Android. But on iPhones, they are restricted to selected countries like India, Malaysia, Saudi Arabia, and Singapore. Check out </span><a rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" href="https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/16669189?hl=en&amp;ref_topic=16669490"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Google’s complete country list</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> before you plan to create yours. </span></p>
<h2 id="how-to-set-up-click-to-whatsapp-on-google-ads-step-by-step"><b>How to Set Up Click to WhatsApp on Google Ads: Step-by-Step</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Once your account is eligible for message assets, you can easily add a WhatsApp button to your Google Ads. Below is a step-by-step procedure you need to follow: </span></p>
<h3 id="step-1-sign-in-to-your-google-ads-account"><b>Step 1: Sign In to Your Google Ads Account</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Go to </span><a rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" href="https://business.google.com/in/google-ads"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Google Ads</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> and sign in to your account. Make sure your account meets all of Google’s eligibility requirements for message assets. </span></p>
<h3 id="step-2-navigate-to-the-assets-menu"><b>Step 2: Navigate to the Assets Menu</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">In the left-hand side menu, tap on Ads &amp; assets and select “Assets”. Now tap on the blue “+” button to create a new asset. </span></p>
<h3 id="step-3-create-a-message-asset"><b>Step 3: Create a Message Asset</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">From the list of available assets, select Message asset. Here, you get the option to attach the asset at one of the three levels: </span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Account level:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Applies to all eligible campaigns.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Campaign level:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Applies only to a specific campaign.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Ad group level:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Applies to a specific ad group.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For most businesses running a Google Click-to-WhatsApp ad, the campaign level is the best option. Why? Because it gives better control over targeting and performance. </span></p>
<h3 id="step-4-add-your-whatsapp-details"><b>Step 4: Add Your WhatsApp Details</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Choose </span><b>WhatsApp </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">as your messaging platform. After that, pick your country and enter your active WhatsApp Business number. </span></p>
<h3 id="step-5-write-the-starter-message-and-cta"><b>Step 5: Write the Starter Message and CTA</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Add a call-to-action (CTA) like Chat Now or Get Quote. Once done, write a starter or welcome message that will appear automatically when users land on the WhatsApp chat window.</span></p>
<p><b>Example:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> “Hey, I’d like to know more about your service or product.” </span></p>
<h3 id="step-5-save-and-review"><b>Step 5: Save and Review</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Check all the details carefully and tap the “Save” button to submit your message asset for Google review. Once it gets approved, the WhatsApp button will appear alongside your search ads. </span></p>
<h2 id="how-much-do-click-to-whatsapp-ads-cost-on-google-ads"><b>How Much Do Click-to-WhatsApp Ads Cost on Google Ads?</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">There is no fixed cost for Click-to-WhatsApp Google Ads. It mainly operates on a dynamic pay-per-click (PPC) auction system. This means you pay Google each time someone taps or clicks on your ads. The cost varies based on industry, keyword demand, targeted location, and campaign type.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Here are the two cost factors to plan for:</span></p>
<div class="table-responsive"><table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><b>Cost</b></td>
<td><b>What it covers</b></td>
<td><b>What sets the price</b></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><span style="font-weight: 400;">Ad cost</span></td>
<td><span style="font-weight: 400;">Clicks on your ad or message button</span></td>
<td><span style="font-weight: 400;">Your bid goal, keywords, and competition, same as any Google Ads campaign</span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><span style="font-weight: 400;">Messaging cost</span></td>
<td><span style="font-weight: 400;">Chats sent through the WhatsApp Business API</span></td>
<td><span style="font-weight: 400;">Your provider&#8217;s rates and how many messages you send each month</span></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The free WhatsApp Business app works fine for limited chats per day. But once your business needs to handle a large volume of leads, the </span><a href="/auth/register"><span style="font-weight: 400;">WhatsApp Business API</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> is worth the cost.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For businesses looking to scale WhatsApp lead generation, HelloBotz combines the WhatsApp Business API, chatbot, </span><a href="/auth/register"><span style="font-weight: 400;">shared team inbox</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">, and WhatsApp automation features to help convert more ad clicks into customers.</span></p>
<h2 id="best-practices-for-click-to-whatsapp-on-google-ads"><b>Best Practices for Click-to-WhatsApp on Google Ads</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">A simple or slight change can make a huge change in the performance of your click-to-WhatsApp on Google Ads: </span></p>
<h3 id="before-you-launch"><b>Before You Launch</b></h3>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Target keywords that show users are actively looking for your product or service. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Keep “WhatsApp” out of your headline, as a headline click will take users to your website, not the chat window. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Match your starter message with your ad. For example, if your ad is about “sports equipment”, don’t start with generic words like &#8221; How can I help you instead, be specific. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Always add action-driven phrases like Chat now or Book an appointment. </span></li>
</ul>
<h3 id="after-you-launch"><b>After You Launch</b></h3>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Use a </span><a href="/auth/register"><span style="font-weight: 400;">WhatsApp Chatbot </span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">to send an instant reply to leads. The faster the reply is, the better the chances of converting leads into customers. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Regularly review the keywords triggering your ads and remove the irrelevant searches. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Measure how many WhatsApp chats turn into qualified leads, bookings, or sales, </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Experiment with headlines, descriptions, and CTAs one by one to know what’s working for your brand better and have better impressions. </span></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="conclusion"><b>Conclusion </b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Setting up a Click-to-WhatsApp on Google Ads offers businesses an effective way to turn Google search into a real conversation. Instead of sending users to slow landing pages or filling out long forms, this feature lets users connect with businesses in real-time on WhatsApp with just a tap. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This not only speeds up the customer buying journey but also makes it more convenient. The key to generating high-quality leads while keeping advertising costs under budget is to get the right keywords, create compelling ad copy, optimize your campaign regularly, and offer instant responses.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Whether you’re running an e-commerce store, real estate, healthcare, or automotive, Google Click to WhatsApp ads help you engage with customers when their buying intent is at its highest. But as your campaigns grow, managing conversations efficiently becomes equally important as generating leads. </span></p>
